   },
   "audio": "signal-09/p05.mp3",
   "durationSec": 7.18,
   "srcHash": "5f2da92c35e29ddcc60ecd5c4e81cf29e21d4221"
  },
  {
   "id": "p06",
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "He put out his fire with wet earth. He picked up the goose, who did not like it. And he ran, badly and slowly and with one arm, into the deep trees. The instinct that told him to run was not one he had been built with. He had grown it here.",
